  "description": "Checkpoints (spec §6). state_digest_cases: digest = b64 sha256(cjson([[item_id,revision,head]...] sorted by item_id)), rows with revision 0 excluded. checkpoint: signed with akv1/checkpoint by a current device of membership_events; verify MUST succeed; invalid_checkpoints MUST fail with expect_error. rollback: checkRollback(witnessed, incoming) MUST accept `accept` cases and reject `reject` cases with expect_error. witnessed_history: checkRollback compares checkpoints only, so a client MUST also run checkWitnessedHistory(witnessed, witnessed_log_head, heads, digests) on the history it replayed (heads[i] and digests[i] are the change-log head and state digest after log_seq i, index 0 the empty log): it MUST accept `accept` cases and reject `reject` cases with expect_error. Every case is also accepted by checkRollback against `incoming`, which is what makes the check necessary.",
